112 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (In microgravity, astronauts experience changes in blood flow due to the lack of normal gravitational forces, which can increase the risk of thrombosis during space missions. These changes may not be easily detected in real time, making early diagnosis challenging in space conditions.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
113 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 94 0 R
/E (The risk can also continue after returning to Earth, as the body readapts to gravity, which may lead to further vascular complications or delayed symptoms. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
